---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Necrons Beginner's Guide — Warhammer 40k"
  description="New to Necrons? Learn who they are, how they play, how to paint them (it's easier than you think), and exactly what to buy first."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-12 border-b border-[#2a2a35]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/factions" class="text-sm text-[#4a4855] hover:text-[#8a8590] transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">
        ← All Factions
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6">
        <div class="text-6xl">🤖</div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#c9a84c] text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 font-display">Faction Guide</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Necrons</h1>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            Ancient machine gods sleeping for 60 million years — and now they're waking up angry. 
            One of the best starter factions: beginner-friendly to paint, durable on the table, 
            and iconic as hell.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick stats bar -->
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Playstyle</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">Durable Shooter</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Painting</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-green-400">Easy ✓</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Rules</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Starter Cost</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">~$170–$250</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lore -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">Who are the Necrons?</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg">
        <p>
          Sixty million years ago, the Necrontyr were a dying race — their sun bathed their worlds in radiation, 
          and their lives were miserable and short. Desperate for immortality, they struck a bargain with 
          god-like entities called the C'tan: trade their organic bodies for immortal metal ones.
        </p>
        <p>
          They got what they asked for. Sort of. The transfer stripped away their souls — leaving behind 
          cold, calculating machines that remembered being alive but could no longer feel it. 
          The C'tan got something too: they feasted on the Necrontyr's consciousnesses like energy. 
          It wasn't a fair deal.
        </p>
        <p>
          Eventually the Necrons turned on the C'tan, shattered them into shards, and then 
          retreated into stasis — sleeping in vast tomb worlds while the galaxy moved on without them. 
          Now they're waking up. Their ancient empire predates humanity by tens of millions of years, 
          and they intend to reclaim it.
        </p>
        <p>
          The aesthetic is ancient Egypt meets skeletal robots. Glowing green eyes and gauss weapons, 
          silver metal bodies, and a deeply unsettling calm. They don't rage. They don't fear. 
          They simply <em>are</em> — and they're very, very patient.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Playstyle -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">How they play on the table</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg mb-10">
        <p>
          Necrons are a <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">resilient shooting army</strong>. They're not the fastest faction 
          and they're not the most aggressive, but they're hard to kill — and that's the point.
        </p>
        <p>
          Their signature ability is <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Reanimation Protocols</strong>: at the end of each 
          phase, destroyed models have a chance to stand back up. It's infuriating to play against 
          and deeply satisfying to play with. As a new player, this is a massive advantage — your 
          mistakes are more survivable than most factions.
        </p>
        <p>
          Their gauss weapons are efficient at stripping wounds. Their HQ units (Overlords, 
          Crypteks) provide strong auras that buff nearby units. The army rewards you for 
          keeping things in coherent groups rather than spreading out.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-green-400">Necrons are for you if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✓ You want an army that feels hard to kill</li>
            <li>✓ You like the idea of models coming back from the dead</li>
            <li>✓ You're new and want something forgiving to learn on</li>
            <li>✓ You love the skeletal robot / ancient alien aesthetic</li>
            <li>✓ You want to spend less time painting and more time playing</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-red-400">Maybe look elsewhere if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✗ You want to get in close and smash things in melee</li>
            <li>✗ You want lots of movement tricks and speed</li>
            <li>✗ You want a horde of cheap, expendable troops</li>
            <li>✗ You prefer organic, living aesthetics</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Painting -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">How to paint Necrons</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">The honest answer: Necrons are one of the easiest armies in the game to paint well. Here's why.</p>

      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 mb-10">
        <p>
          The core body is metallic silver — you can basecoat an entire Necron Warrior in one pass 
          with a spray can. One wash of dark contrast medium later and you've got depth and shadow 
          without touching a brush to 90% of the model. The classic Necron scheme is genuinely 
          achievable by a complete beginner on day one.
        </p>
        <p>
          The glowing green energy effects (eyes, weapon coils) are where you can add personality — 
          but even those are optional. A wash of the right contrast paint gets you most of the way there.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Step by step -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-lg mb-4">The classic scheme — step by step</h3>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">1</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Spray with Leadbelcher</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Citadel's metallic silver spray primer. Covers the whole model in 30 seconds. Let it dry fully.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">2</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Wash with Nuln Oil</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">A thin black wash that flows into recesses and creates instant shadow and depth. Apply generously across the whole model.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">3</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Drybrush with Ironbreaker</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Load a dry brush, wipe most of it off on paper, then brush lightly across raised edges. Brings the metal back to life and adds highlights instantly.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">4</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Pick out the eyes and weapon coils</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Load a small brush with Tesseract Glow (a green technical paint). Dab it into the eye sockets and the glowing coils on gauss weapons. It's self-shading — one coat is enough.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">5</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Base the model</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">A texture paint like Astrogranite Debris on the base, a drybrush of Administratum Grey over it, and a static grass tuft. Done.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">
          That's a table-ready Necron Warrior in under 20 minutes. The scheme scales perfectly to an entire army.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- What to buy -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">What to buy first</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-10 text-lg">In order. Don't buy anything else until you've finished step one.</p>

      <!-- Step 1: Combat Patrol -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
          <div>
            <span class="bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-display mr-2">Start Here</span>
            <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$170</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Combat Patrol: Necrons</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          The best entry point for any new Necron player. Includes a Necron Overlord (your commander), 
          10 Necron Warriors (your core troop), Canoptek Scarabs (fast-moving objective grabbers), 
          and a Canoptek Reanimator (support unit that helps your reanimation rolls). 
          It's a legal, playable army out of one box.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.games-workshop.com/en-US/Combat-Patrol-Necrons-2023"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Buy from Games Workshop →
        </a>
        <!-- TODO: replace with Amazon affiliate link once account is set up -->
      </div>

      <!-- Step 2: Extra Warriors -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3">
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$55 · optional first expansion</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Necron Warriors (12-model box)</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          More Warriors means more reanimation rolls — the backbone of how the army plays. 
          If you're having fun after painting the Combat Patrol, this is the natural next box. 
          Gives you two weapon options: gauss flayer (reliable) and gauss reaper (close range).
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.games-workshop.com/en-US/Necron-Warriors-2020"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          View on Games Workshop →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Paints -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">Paints you need</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { name: 'Leadbelcher Spray', use: 'Base coat — covers the whole model', required: true },
            { name: 'Nuln Oil', use: 'Shade wash — instant depth and shadow', required: true },
            { name: 'Ironbreaker', use: 'Drybrush highlight — brings metal back to life', required: true },
            { name: 'Tesseract Glow', use: 'The glowing green eye/weapon effect', required: true },
            { name: 'Astrogranite Debris', use: 'Texture paint for bases', required: false },
            { name: 'Administratum Grey', use: 'Drybrush over basing texture', required: false },
          ].map(paint => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class={`text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 font-display ${paint.required ? 'bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113]' : 'border border-[#2a2a35] text-[#4a4855]'}`}>
                {paint.required ? 'Essential' : 'Optional'}
              </span>
              <div>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold">{paint.name}</span>
                <span class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm"> — {paint.use}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-5 italic">~$35 total for all six. Citadel paints are available at most game stores and online.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Cost breakdown -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-8">Honest cost breakdown</h2>
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        {[
          { item: 'Combat Patrol: Necrons', cost: '~$170', note: 'Playable army out of one box' },
          { item: 'Essential paints (4)', cost: '~$24', note: 'Spray + wash + drybrush + glow' },
          { item: 'Spray primer', cost: 'Included', note: 'Leadbelcher spray is your primer' },
          { item: 'Basing supplies', cost: '~$12', note: 'Texture paint + tuft + grey' },
          { item: 'Clippers + hobby knife', cost: '~$20', note: 'One-time purchase — use forever' },
          { item: 'Superglue', cost: '~$5', note: 'Standard plastic glue works too' },
        ].map((row, i) => (
          <div class={`flex items-start justify-between px-5 py-4 gap-4 ${i % 2 === 0 ? '' : 'bg-[#111113]'}`}>
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold">{row.item}</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-0.5">{row.note}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] flex-shrink-0">{row.cost}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 bg-[#1f1d14] border-t border-[#c9a84c]">
          <p class="font-display font-semibold">All-in starter total</p>
          <span class="font-display font-bold text-[#c9a84c] text-lg">~$230</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">
        Prices approximate and subject to change. Some items (clippers, glue) are reusable forever.
        Third-party paints like Army Painter can cut paint costs by 30–40%.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Next steps CTA -->
  <section class="px-6 py-20 text-center">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold mb-4">Ready to start?</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg mb-8">
        Grab the Combat Patrol, get your four essential paints, and follow the painting steps above. 
        You'll have a painted, playable army faster than you think.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a
          href="/painting"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display tracking-wide"
        >
          Painting Guide →
        </a>
        <a
          href="/quiz"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Retake the Quiz
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
